Q: CSS, HTML: Sidebar with animation as 1 button not as 2 A: <pre><code>The reason you see “20 buttons” instead of 10 is that your code currently has two separate divs:
</code></pre>
<ol>
<li><p><code>.buttons</code> → the side “icon” bar.</p>
</li>
<li><p><code>.sidenav</code> → the slide-out menu.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p>Since both contain the same <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> elements, opening the menu effectively <strong>duplicates the buttons visually</strong>.</p>
<hr />
<h3><strong>Solution: Use only one set of buttons</strong></h3>
<p>Instead of duplicating buttons, keep <strong>all buttons in the sidenav</strong> and use <strong>CSS + JS</strong> to control what’s visible when the menu is open or closed.<br />
<strong>Example HTML:</strong></p>
<pre><code>&lt;div id=&quot;mySidenav&quot; class=&quot;sidenav&quot;&gt;
  &lt;a&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;B&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text&quot;&gt;Button 1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;a&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;B&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text&quot;&gt;Button 2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;a&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;B&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text&quot;&gt;Button 3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;!-- more buttons --&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;span class=&quot;menu-toggle&quot; onclick=&quot;MenuButton()&quot;&gt;M&lt;/span&gt;
</code></pre>
<p><strong>CSS:</strong></p>
<pre><code>.sidenav {
  height: 100%;
  width: 50px; /* closed width, show only icons */
  position: fixed;
  top: 34px;
  left: 0;
  background-color: #111;
  overflow-x: hidden;
  transition: width 0.3s;
  padding-top: 14px;
}

.sidenav a {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  padding: 8px;
  color: white;
  text-decoration: none;
  transition: 0.3s;
}

.sidenav a .text {
  margin-left: 10px;
  opacity: 0; /* hide text when menu is closed */
  transition: opacity 0.3s;
}

.sidenav.open {
  width: 150px; /* full width when open */
}

.sidenav.open a .text {
  opacity: 1; /* show text when open */
}
</code></pre>
<p><strong>JavaScript:</strong></p>
<pre><code>function MenuButton() {
  const sidenav = document.getElementById(&quot;mySidenav&quot;);
  sidenav.classList.toggle(&quot;open&quot;);
}
</code></pre>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
